# {{.Name}}

> A PlatformKit application: one Go binary composing a nine-module multi-tenant
> SaaS starter (auth, users, tenants, API keys, audit, content, notifications,
> health, admin console) plus your own modules. Server-rendered HTML, no Node.

Extend it with `platformkit new module <name>`, which generates a
self-registering, tenant-scoped module. Read AGENTS.md before writing code —
it is the contract that keeps generated code correct.

## Key files

- [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md): the rules for extending the app safely (tenant
  scoping, server-owned identity, per-route authz, canonical entity IDs,
  append-only migrations). Read this first.
- [main.go](main.go): boots the starter via `starterapp.Run` with the
  registered modules.
- [modules.go](modules.go): the additive module registry.
- [Makefile](Makefile): `make verify` is the gate (`go vet` + `go test -race`).
- [config.example.yaml](config.example.yaml): deployment config; the admin
  password comes from `PK_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, never the file.

## Commands

- `go run .` — boot a development instance at http://127.0.0.1:8080/admin
- `platformkit new module <name>` — scaffold a tenant-scoped module
- `platformkit modules --json` — list composed modules
- `platformkit openapi` — the OpenAPI document
- `make verify` — vet + race tests

## Rules that generated code already follows

- Every store query is scoped `WHERE tenant_id = ?`; by-id is `id AND tenant_id`.
- The server binds tenant and owner from the principal (`portslib.RequestActor`);
  the request body's tenant_id is ignored.
- Every route checks a scope (`<name>:read` / `<name>:write`; admin passes).
- Path IDs are canonical `id-<hex>` segments via `portslib.EntityIDFromPath`.
- Migrations are append-only.
